<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Sambians</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1255 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Prussian people of the Sambian peninsula, the world's richest source of Baltic amber, whose conquest in 1255 led to the founding of Königsberg.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Sambians lived on the Sambian peninsula between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> and Curonian lagoons, in today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaliningrad-oblast">Kaliningrad</a> region. Their amber had reached the Roman world, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> Scandinavian traders settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiskiauten">Wiskiauten</a> nearby. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adam-of-bremen">Adam of Bremen</a> in the 11th century described the Sambians as humane people with much fur.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Sambia was the most populous and wealthy Prussian land, with nobles holding fortified seats and a strong warrior class. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jaipur-state">Amber</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a> and slaves were traded across the Baltic. The Sambians kept the Prussian pagan religion and resisted Danish and Polish missions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1255 a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">King Ottokar II of Bohemia</a> subdued Sambia, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a>, named in his honour. The Sambians rose again from 1260 under Glande but were defeated. Many nobles joined the Order's service, and their land became Order territory and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bishopric-of-samland">Bishopric of Samland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sambians.jpg" alt="Sambians" width="320" height="225"><figcaption>Image: Renata3 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prussian_clans_13th_century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1255 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Glande</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Baltic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Prussian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sambia, Semba</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1028&amp;focus=sambians" aria-label="Sambians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5637 186 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sambians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5451 561h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5957 442h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5957 442h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Russia. <a href="/atlas?year=1028&amp;focus=sambians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

